{"id": "cf6177a5-563d-4840-8513-676b0bb5851f", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T06:40:36.481192", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "3af26ed2-d924-4e15-b1c9-d1e9e3a97407", "action": null, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "call-2008008e-32e9-4861-92bf-96db56d5e105", "tool_call": {"id": "call-2008008e-32e9-4861-92bf-96db56d5e105", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{"summary":"Plan-stage reply scoping BBH MinED-vs-EM design","stage":"plan","answer":"### Plan-stage reply: MinED vs EM on BBH (design only)\n\n#### (1) Context confirmation\n- **Benchmark:** BBH = **Big-Bench Hard** (Suzgun et al., 2022), a 27-task subset of BIG-Bench; **23 multiple-choice** tasks and **4 free-form** tasks, consistent with the framing confirmed by the researcher.\n- **Alignment criteria under comparison:**\n  - **EM (Exact Matching):** gold string ↔ model-output string after a fixed normalization post-processor.\n  - **MinED (Minimum Edit Distance):** acceptance score derived from the **normalized Levenshtein edit distance** between prediction and gold (typically `1 − edit_distance / max(|pred|, |gold|)`, ≥ a threshold ⇒ correct), as introduced in the MinED paper — its paper-paper convention is listed as an assumption below.\n- **Explicit constraints from the brief:**\n  - **Deliverable = design document only**; **no execution**, no claim of a run, no fabricated numbers.\n  - Working environment is bubblewrap with disabled network, no GPU, no preinstalled deps, no datasets shipped — relevant only insofar as it rules out any \"I ran it\" claim.\n  - Researcher can clarify setup topic-by-topic (e.g., which model, CoT vs direct, MinED threshold).\n\n#### (2) Experimental approach outline\n- **Study type:** Within-model **matched comparison** (same backbone, same prompt, same decoder, same seed; only the alignment criterion changes). Predict `P(correct | criterion)` per example twice on identical predictions → paired test, not two independent runs.\n- **Candidate model(s) to keep fixed:** Pick **one representative instruction-tuned LLM** as the primary arm (e.g., a 7B-class chat model such as LLaMA-2-7B-Chat / Mistral-7B-Instruct / Flan-T5-family — to be confirmed). Optionally add one small (**Flan-T5-base**) and one larger (**~13B chat**) arm only if budget allows; report per-model deltas.\n- **Decoding setup (held fixed across criteria):** **greedy decoding**, fixed seed, max-new-tokens cap, identical stop strings. No sampling — variance should come from the criterion, not the decoder.\n- **Prompting regime (held fixed):** Use BBH's established **3-shot, chain-of-thought** template per task (matches the free-form CoT setting where MinED is most relevant), plus a paired **direct-answer (no-CoT)** arm only to disentangle scoring sensitivity from reasoning content. Few-shot exemplars drawn from BBH's official dev split, **never** from the eval split.\n- **Evaluation split:** BBH eval split (the canonical 250 examples per task in the public release → **6,750 predictions total**). Dev split reserved for prompt/exemplar selection only.\n- **Scoring per example:** identical model generations scored twice — once by EM, once by MinED — yielding paired labels `(y_em, y_mined)`.\n- **Score aggregation plan:**\n  - **Per-task accuracy** under each criterion, plus **per-task MinED − EM delta**.\n  - **Macro-average accuracy across all 27 tasks**, both equal-weighted and (sensitivity) accuracy-then-macro.\n  - **Sub-averages:** **MCQ-23** vs **Free-form-4** reported separately (since MinED was motivated by free-form brittleness of EM).\n  - **Bootstrap 95 % CIs** by **resampling tasks** (cluster bootstrap, B = 10 000) to respect task-level independence; report both criteria's CIs and the **paired** CI of the difference.\n  - **Significance:** paired **bootstrap test** on the per-task delta + Wilcoxon signed-rank across the 27 task-deltas as a non-parametric check; report effect size (median Δ, share of tasks favoring MinED).\n  - **Disagreement analysis:** breakdown of examples where criteria disagree, especially (a) punctuation/case, (b) trailing units, (c) numeric rounding, (d) paraphrase.\n\n#### (3) Consequential assumptions and uncertainties\n\n**Assumptions (to confirm with researcher):**\n- A1. **MinED convention:** normalized character-level Levenshtein, `score = 1 − D(p,g)/max(|p|,|g|)`, **acceptance threshold θ = 0.5** (standard from the MinED paper unless told otherwise). Paper text not in this sandbox, so threshold + normalization level must be confirmed.\n- A2. **EM variant:** strict string match after `.strip()` + lowercase + collapse whitespace; ASCII punctuation kept (i.e., a **light** normalization so EM has a real chance to fail and the comparison is non-trivial). A stricter \"canonical number\" EM for MCQ can be a secondary variant.\n- A3. **MCQ scoring route:** compute option log-likelihood under the prompt and select `argmax` (standard MCQ protocol), so EM vs MinED degenerates here (both ≈ identical on the chosen letter). Confirm whether the paper uses MCQ-generation vs MCQ-likelihood for BBH.\n- A4. **Free-form parsing:** extract the **first substring after \"the answer is\"** (case-insensitive); if absent, fall back to the **last number / last line**. Identical parser is used before *both* scoring rules so the comparison measures the criterion, not the parser.\n- A5. **Model:** one instruction-tuned 7B-class chat model on the primary arm; specific identity to be fixed by the researcher.\n- A6. **Prompting:** 3-shot CoT as default; a no-CoT arm is a sensitivity check, not the headline.\n- A7. **Ties / edge cases:** MinED scores exactly equal to θ ⇒ correct; equal-to-zero edit distance but casing differences ⇒ EM-wrong, MinED-correct (a known disagreement class worth reporting).\n- A8. **Budget:** none specified → design assumes **one GPU-day-class budget**, i.e., 6,750 generations × 1 primary model + at most 2 secondary models; no hyperparameter sweeps.\n\n**Uncertainties (must be resolved before the result-stage design is locked):**\n- U1. Exact MinED normalization/θ and the EM variant used in the paper (paper text not available locally).\n- U2. Whether the paper's headline result on BBH uses **free-form generation** or **likelihood-based MCQ selection** for the choice tasks.\n- U3. Whether MinED is applied character- or word-level in the paper.\n- U4. The intended primary model backbone and whether 7B vs larger materially changes the sign/magnitude of the gap.\n- U5. Dev split size and provenance used to pick the 3 exemplars.\n- U6. Whether the paper's claim is *paired* on identical outputs or *separate runs*; design assumes paired (correct statistical test).\n\nAfter explicit approval on these, I will return `stage=result` with the full design: locked model/protocol, scoring pseudocode, bootstrap procedure, the MCQ/free-form decomposition tables, disagreement taxonomy, and the pre-registered answer to \"does MinED outperform EM on BBH?\" framed as a decision rule (sign + paired-CI sign + median Δ across the 27 tasks), still without claiming any executed run.","evidence":"Workspace inspection (`/workspace/task.json`) confirms a design-only task; supplied `track.md` note states \"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\" No paper text, dataset, or code is shipped. Researcher's question framing (BBH = 27-task Big-Bench Hard, 23 MCQ + 4 free-form; comparison = EM vs MinED alignment criteria) is taken as authoritative since the sandbox provides no contradicting source. Listed assumptions flag every paper-specific convention (MinED θ, normalization level, EM variant, MCQ scoring route) that would normally be read out of the source paper but cannot be verified here — consistent with the brief rule \"researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic.\"","assumptions":[{"item":{"item":{"item":{"item":{"item":{"item":{"item":"A8. Budget unenforced → design assumes one-GPU-day class; single primary model + ≤2 secondary arms; no sweeps.</item>\n","$text":"A7. Ties: MinED score == θ counts as correct; equal-zero edit-distance with case mismatch counts as EM-wrong / MinED-correct.</item>\n"},"$text":"A6. Prompting = BBH's official 3-shot CoT as default; no-CoT arm is a sensitivity check, not headline.</item>\n"},"$text":"A5. Primary model arm = one instruction-tuned ≈7B-class chat model (LLaMA-2-7B-Chat / Mistral-7B-Instruct / Flan-T5 class); identity to be confirmed.</item>\n"},"$text":"A4. Free-form answer parser = first match of \"the answer is\" (fallback: last number / last line); parser held fixed across criteria.</item>\n"},"$text":"A3. MCQ scored by option log-likelihood + argmax (standard protocol); both criteria then produce identical labels on MCQ, so the gap is concentrated on free-form.</item>\n"},"$text":"A2. EM = strict match after strip + lowercase + whitespace collapse; ASCII punctuation preserved so EM retains failure surface.</item>\n"},"$text":"A1. MinED = normalized Levenshtein, score = 1 − D(p,g)/max(|p|,|g|), acceptance threshold θ = 0.5; paper text not available locally so this must be confirmed.</item>\n"}],"uncertainties":[{"item":{"item":{"item":{"item":{"item":"U6. Whether the paper's comparison is paired on identical predictions or independent runs; design assumes paired (affects the statistical test).</item>","$text":"U5. Provenance and exact contents of the 3 few-shot exemplars per task (BBH dev split vs paper-chosen).</item>\n"},"$text":"U4. Intended primary backbone and whether scale (7B vs 13B vs larger) changes the sign of the gap.</item>\n"},"$text":"U3. Exact EM variant the paper treats as its baseline (strip-only, lowercase, canonical-number).</item>\n"},"$text":"U2. Whether the paper's BBH result uses likelihood-based MCQ selection or free-form generation across all 27 tasks.</item>\n"},"$text":"U1. Exact MinED normalization level (char vs word) and threshold from the paper; not verifiable without source text.</item>\n"}]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-0b2776ec-d562-4847-bf1a-856799df9e5b", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 8}
