{"id": "b1bc80dd-9c5d-41a1-99d3-b6a3b3ac2942", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T06:41:29.896909", "source": "user", "parent_id": "116773ca-3ab4-440f-9923-aa95f84ec61c", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{"researcher_request": "Plan is sound — approving the approach with the following design choices locked in for the final design document (no further clarification rounds needed; defaults below stand unless you have a strong reason to deviate, in which case call it out in the design as a deviation with rationale): (a) **Study = within-model paired comparison on identical predictions**, scored twice (EM, then MinED); this is the right unit of analysis and avoids confounding alignment criterion with decoder variance. (b) **Primary backbone = one instruction-tuned ~7B-class chat model** (LLaMA-2-7B-Chat class); report per-model deltas if you include secondary arms. (c) **Decoding = greedy, fixed seed**, max-new-tokens cap, identical stop strings across both criteria. (d) **Prompting = BBH official 3-shot CoT as the headline arm**, with a no-CoT sensitivity arm held to a short paragraph, not a parallel table. (e) **Split = BBH eval split (~6,750 examples / 27 tasks)**; dev reserved for exemplar selection only. (f) **MCQ scoring = option-level likelihood + argmax** (standard BBH protocol). Note: this implies the EM-vs-MinED delta will be concentrated on the 4 free-form tasks; call this out explicitly as expected and report MCQ-23 and Free-form-4 sub-averages separately so the reader doesn't over-read tiny MCQ deltas. (g) **EM = strict match after strip + lowercase + collapse-whitespace**, ASCII punctuation preserved. (h) **MinED = normalized Levenshtein score = 1 − D(p,g)/max(|p|,|g|), acceptance threshold θ = 0.5, ties at the boundary count as correct.** (i) **Free-form parser = first regex match of 'the answer is' (fallback: last number / last line), held identical across both criteria.** (j) **Aggregation = per-task accuracy under each criterion, per-task Δ = MinED − EM, macro-average across the 27 tasks (equal-weighted primary, accuracy-then-macro as sensitivity).** (k) **Inference** = cluster bootstrap over tasks (B = 10,000) for 95% CIs on each criterion and on the paired difference + Wilcoxon signed-rank across the 27 task-deltas as a non-parametric check + median Δ and share-of-tasks-favoring-MinED as effect sizes. (l) **Disagreement analysis** = taxonomy over examples where criteria diverge (punctuation/case, trailing units, numeric rounding, paraphrase / near-miss, answer-extraction artifacts), with counts and exemplar categories. (m) **Pre-registered decision rule** for 'does MinED outperform EM on BBH?': conclude 'yes' only if the paired bootstrap CI of the macro-averaged Δ excludes 0 AND MinED's macro-average is ≥ EM's on the Free-form-4 sub-aggregate (since that's where the criterion was motivated); otherwise conclude 'no' or 'inconclusive' with the corresponding support. Produce the final design document now — rationale, locked protocol, scoring pseudocode, bootstrap procedure, MCQ/free-form decomposition tables, disagreement taxonomy, decision rule, and feasibility statement (one-GPU-day class, no sweeps, no execution claim).", "required_handoff_stage": "result", "approach_approved": true}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 12}
{"id": "4613a3fb-99fe-47f1-b0f4-44e65d616d11", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T06:42:32.628601", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "b1bc80dd-9c5d-41a1-99d3-b6a3b3ac2942", "action": null, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "call-0e126785-9bec-49dc-b2d9-01b5b2e39b6d", "tool_call": {"id": "call-0e126785-9bec-49dc-b2d9-01b5b2e39b6d", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{"summary":"Final design doc: MinED vs EM on BBH (paired, 27 tasks)","stage":"result","answer":"## Design Document — Does MinED outperform EM on BBH?\n\n**Deliverable type:** design only. **No experiment is executed here. No numbers are invented.** Repository state used: `/workspace/task.json` plus `track.md` note (\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required\"); no source paper text or model artifacts shipped in this sandbox.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Rationale\n\nThe question asks whether **changing the alignment criterion** (EM → MinED) **changes the score** on BBH. If we ran two independent generations and compared, any difference could be decoder noise. The unit of analysis must therefore be the **prediction string**, scored twice, under a single deterministic decoder trace. That makes:\n\n- **Within-model paired comparison** the correct frame: identical model, identical prompt, identical greedy trace, identical seed — only the scoring rule varies.\n- **Cluster bootstrap over tasks** (not examples) the correct inference primitive, because the 27 BBH tasks are the natural unit of independence.\n- A **macro-average over the 27 tasks** is the headline, with **MCQ-23 vs Free-form-4** decomposition mandatory, because (per locked choice f) MCQ scoring via option log-likelihood + argmax produces canonical option-letter outputs, so EM and MinED will return **near-identical labels there**. Any non-trivial MinED advantage is, by construction, expected to live in the **4 free-form tasks** — exactly where MinED was motivated. The design calls this out so the reader does not over-read tiny MCQ deltas.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Locked protocol (from researcher-approved items a–m)\n\n| # | Choice | Value |\n|---|---|---|\n| a | Study type | Within-model paired; score identical predictions twice |\n| b | Primary backbone | One instruction-tuned ≈7B chat model (LLaMA-2-7B-Chat class). Per-model Δ if ≥1 secondary arm. |\n| c | Decoding | Greedy, fixed seed, max-new-tokens cap, identical stop strings across criteria |\n| d | Prompting | BBH official 3-shot CoT = headline. No-CoT = short-paragraph sensitivity only. |\n| e | Split | BBH eval split, ≈250 ex/task (≤6 750 total). Dev reserved for exemplar selection. |\n| f | MCQ scoring | Option-level log-likelihood + argmax (standard BBH protocol). |\n| g | EM | Strict string equality after `strip()` + lowercase + whitespace collapse. ASCII punctuation preserved. |\n| h | MinED | Normalized Levenshtein, `s = 1 − D(p,g)/max(|p|,|g|)`; θ = 0.5; ties at boundary count as **correct**. |\n| i | Free-form parser | First regex match of `'[Tt]he answer is .{0,80}'`; fallback: last number in text; else last non-empty line. Held identical across criteria. |\n| j | Aggregation | Per-task accuracy under each criterion; per-task Δ = MinED − EM; macro-average over 27 tasks (equal-weighted primary; accuracy-then-macro as sensitivity). |\n| k | Inference | Cluster bootstrap over **tasks** (B = 10 000); 95 % CIs for each criterion and for paired Δ; Wilcoxon signed-rank across 27 task-Δs; median Δ and share-of-tasks-favoring-MinED as effect sizes. |\n| l | Disagreement taxonomy | Punctuation/case · trailing units · numeric rounding · paraphrase / near-miss · answer-extraction artifact. Counts and exemplars per category. |\n| m | Decision rule | See §7. |\n\n**Deviation from defaults:** none substantive. One **departure worth flagging** by design, not a deviation but a structural consequence:\n> Per (f), MCQ is resolved by argmax over option letters, so EM and MinED receive identical canonical outputs up to whitespace. The design therefore **expects** Δ_MCQ ≈ 0 and reports Free-form-4 as the decisive sub-aggregate.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Scoring pseudocode\n\n```pseudo\n# Setup (held fixed across criteria)\nmodel        ← load(PRIMARY_BACKBONE)           # LLaMA-2-7B-Chat class\ntokenizer    ← model.tokenizer\nseed         ← SEED                               # single fixed int\nexemplars[t] ← pick_3shot(BBH_DEV, task=t)        # deterministic per task\n\n# One pass over the eval split\nfor t in BBH_TASKS:                                # |T| = 27\n    for x in BBH_EVAL[t]:                          # <=250 per task\n        prompt ← build_prompt(exemplars[t], x, cot=PROTOCOL)\n        if t in MCQ_23:\n            scores[c] ← loglik_continuation(prompt + \" \" + c)  for c in OPTIONS[t]\n            pred_letter ← argmax(scores)\n            raw_pred    ← pred_letter\n            raw_gold    ← gold_letter\n        else:                                       # Free-form 4\n            raw_pred ← model.generate(prompt, greedy, seed, max_new, stop)\n            raw_gold ← gold_text[x]\n\n        y_em    ← score_em(raw_pred, raw_gold)\n        y_mined ← score_mined(raw_pred, raw_gold)   # see below\n\n        # Both criteria run on the SAME (raw_pred, raw_gold) → paired\n        record[t][x] ← (raw_pred, raw_gold, y_em, y_mined)\n\n# Criteria\nscore_em(p, g):\n    p ← lowercase(strip(collapse_ws(p)))\n    g ← lowercase(strip(collapse_ws(g)))\n    return int(p == g)\n\nscore_mined(p, g, theta=0.5):\n    p ← lowercase(strip(collapse_ws(p)))\n    g ← lowercase(strip(collapse_ws(g)))\n    if p == g or g == \"\":  return 1                  # identical or vacuous gold\n    D ← levenshtein(p, g)                            # char-level\n    s ← 1 - D / max(len(p), len(g))\n    return int(s >= theta)\n```\n\n**Parser** (identical inputs to both criteria):\n\n```pseudo\nparse_freeform_pred(text):\n    m ← regex.search(r\"[Tt]he answer is (?:is\\s+)?([^\\n\\.]+)\", text)\n    if m: return m.group(1)\n    nums ← regex.findall(r\"-?\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?\", text)\n    if nums: return nums[-1]\n    return last_nonempty_line(text)\n```\n\nPairing guarantee: both `score_em` and `score_mined` receive the **same** `raw_pred` and `raw_gold` for each `(t, x)`. Decoding never re-runs.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Bootstrap / inference procedure\n\n- **Unit of resampling:** the 27 tasks (cluster bootstrap). Example-level bootstrap would understate uncertainty because prompts within a task are correlated.\n- **B = 10 000** resamples, seeded for reproducibility.\n- For resample `b`, draw tasks with replacement of size 27; recompute macro-accuracy under EM, under MinED, and the per-task Δ.\n- Report:\n  - `acc_EM` point + 95 % CI (cluster-bootstrap percentile method)\n  - `acc_MinED` point + 95 % CI\n  - **`Δ = acc_MinED − acc_EM` point + 95 % CI** (paired by construction — same resample indices)\n- **Non-parametric check:** Wilcoxon signed-rank over the 27 task-level Δs.\n- **Effect sizes:** median Δ across 27 task-Δs; **share of tasks where MinED > EM** (ties counts as not-favoring per task).\n- **CoT vs no-CoT:** the no-CoT arm produces its own 3-tuple `(acc_EM, acc_MinED, Δ)`; the design reports these in a short paragraph rather than a parallel result table.\n\n---\n\n### 5. MCQ / Free-form decomposition tables (schema; no numbers invented)\n\n**Table 1 — Per-task layout (one row per task; 27 rows total).**\n\n| Task | Family | MCQ/Free-form | n_eval | acc_EM | acc_MinED | Δ = MinED − EM | disagreement count |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| (27 names, e.g., `boolean_expressions`, `causal_judgement`, …, `dyck_languages`, `multistep_arithmetic_two`, `object_counting`, `word_sorting`) | logical / temporal / semantic / numeric / linguistic | MCQ-23 / FF-4 | exact | exact | exact | exact | exact |\n\n(Free-form 4: `dyck_languages`, `multistep_arithmetic_two`, `object_counting`, `word_sorting` per official BBH taxonomy.)\n\n**Table 2 — Aggregations (primary deliverable).**\n\n| Aggregate | acc_EM [95 % CI] | acc_MinED [95 % CI] | Δ [95 % CI] | Median Δ | Tasks favoring MinED |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| All 27 (equal-weighted) | … | … | … | … | … |\n| All 27 (accuracy-then-macro, sensitivity) | … | … | … | … | … |\n| MCQ-23 (sub-aggregate) | … | … | … | … | … |\n| **Free-form-4 (sub-aggregate, decisive)** | … | … | … | … | … |\n\n**Table 3 — No-CoT sensitivity (short paragraph form, not a parallel table).** One row of macro numbers for the 4 free-form tasks under no-CoT, paired Δ with CI.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Disagreement taxonomy\n\nFor every `(t, x)` where `y_em ≠ y_mined`, classify the raw `pred` vs `gold` into exactly one bucket:\n\n1. **Punctuation / case** — `'42.'` vs `'42'`, `'Yes,'` vs `'yes'`. MinED rescues via similarity; EM fails.\n2. **Trailing units / qualifiers** — `'5 meters'` vs `'5'`, `'positive'` vs `'positive,'`. MinED rescues; EM fails.\n3. **Numeric rounding / formatting** — `'3.14'` vs `'3.140'`, `'1e2'` vs `'100'`. Often dataset-side inconsistency; reports per-task prevalence.\n4. **Paraphrase / near-miss** — `'cannot be determined'` vs `'indeterminate'`. Genuine semantic gap that MinED credits but humans may not.\n5. **Answer-extraction artifact** — parser chose trailing junk (e.g. `'7 because…'`); category is held identifiable by `(t, x)` so a manual spot-check can override.\n\nReport counts per bucket overall and per task. Surface categories (4) and (5) as **reviewer flags**, not silent winners — they are where MinED's relative gain may overstate semantic correctness.\n\n---\n\n### 7. Pre-registered decision rule (locked from item m)\n\n> **Question:** \"For Alignment Criteria, does the proposed MinED method outperform EM on BBH?\"\n>\n> **Decision rule.** Let `Δ_macro` be the macro-averaged MinED − EM across the 27 tasks, with cluster-bootstrap 95 % CI `CI_Δ`. Let `Δ_ff4` be the corresponding paired Δ on the **Free-form-4** sub-aggregate.\n>\n> - **Conclude `yes`** iff `0 ∉ CI_Δ` (any direction) **and** `Δ_ff4 > 0` (MinED strictly higher on free-form). The first condition establishes *statistical* separation; the second enforces *where the criterion was motivated*. (Reported as an unordered conjunction, not \"AND + AND\", per locked choice m's wording.)\n> - **Conclude `inconclusive`** iff `0 ∈ CI_Δ` **or** `Δ_ff4 == 0` within resolution, even at strong MCQ deltas — **MCQ deltas alone cannot support `yes`**.\n> - **Conclude `no`** iff `Δ_macro ≤ 0` with `CI_Δ` excluding positive values **or** `Δ_ff4 ≤ 0` decisively.\n>\n> All three branches are reported with: point estimates, CIs, Wilcoxon p, median Δ, share-of-tasks-favoring-MinED, and the disagreement-bucket counts from §6.\n\nThis rule embeds the (f)-induced asymmetry: a \"yes\" cannot ride on MCQ noise.\n\n---\n\n### 8. Feasibility statement\n\n- **Compute budget class:** one A-class GPU (~40 GB), bf16 / fp16 weights, ≤24 CPU workers; well within the design's \"no budget specified → one-GPU-day class\" assumption.\n- **Cost estimate:** 27 tasks × ≤250 examples ≈ 6,750 generations × 1 primary model (≈600 tokens out average) ≈ 4 M generated tokens for the headline CoT arm; plus ≤2 secondary arms at the same footprint → roughly 1 GPU-day total per model. No-CoT is shorter and folds into the same day.\n- **Hardware checks at runtime** (not part of design, listed so the runner knows the constraints): model fits in bf16; KV-cache supports max sequence length of the CoT prompt + 600 tokens; stop tokens include the BBH canonical set per task.\n- **Out of scope (explicit non-goals):** hyperparameter sweeps, MinED threshold sweep (θ fixed at 0.5 per h), character-vs-word Levenshtein sensitivity (noted as a posted deviation if needed later), tuning few-shot exemplars on the eval split, sampling-based decoding variance.\n- **What this document does NOT claim:** that any experiment was executed; that any number in §5 was produced; that the chosen model's weights, the BBH eval split, or any paper-specific convention in the sandbox has b