l MinED advantage is, by construction, expected to live in the **4 free-form tasks** \u2014 exactly where MinED was motivated. The design calls this out so the reader does not over-read tiny MCQ deltas.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Locked protocol (from researcher-approved items a\u2013m)\n\n| # | Choice | Value |\n|---|---|---|\n| a | Study type | Within-model paired; score identical predictions twice |\n| b | Primary backbone | One instruction-tuned \u22487B chat model (LLaMA-2-7B-Chat class). Per-model \u0394 if \u22651 secondary arm. |\n| c | Decoding | Greedy, fixed seed, max-new-tokens cap, identical stop strings across criteria |\n| d | Prompting | BBH official 3-shot CoT = headline. No-CoT = short-paragraph sensitivity only. |\n| e | Split | BBH eval split, \u2248250 ex/task (\u22646 750 total). Dev reserved for exemplar selection. |\n| f | MCQ scoring | Option-level log-likelihood + argmax (standard BBH protocol). |\n| g | EM | Strict string equality after `strip()` + lowercase + whitespace collapse. ASCII punctuation preserved. |\n| h | MinED | Normalized Levenshtein, `s = 1 \u2212 D(p,g)/max(|p|,|g|)`; \u03b8 = 0.5; ties at boundary count as **correct**. |\n| i | Free-form parser | First regex match of `'[Tt]he answer is .{0,80}'`; fallback: last number in text; else last non-empty line. Held identical across criteria. |\n| j | Aggregation | Per-task accuracy under each criterion; per-task \u0394 = MinED \u2212 EM; macro-average over 27 tasks (equal-weighted primary; accuracy-then-macro as sensitivity). |\n| k | Inference | Cluster bootstrap over **tasks** (B = 10 000); 95 % CIs for each criterion and for paired \u0394; Wilcoxon signed-rank across 27 task-\u0394s; median \u0394 and share-of-tasks-favoring-MinED as effect sizes. |\n| l | Disagreement taxonomy | Punctuation/case \u00b7 trailing units \u00b7 numeric rounding \u00b7 paraphrase / near-miss \u00b7 answer-extraction artifact. Counts and exemplars per category. |\n| m | Decision rule | See \u00a77. |\n\n**Departure worth flagging (structural, not a deviation):** Per (f), MCQ is resolved by argmax over option letters, so EM and MinED receive identical canonical outputs up to whitespace. The design therefore **expects** \u0394_MCQ \u2248 0 and reports Free-form-4 as the decisive sub-aggregate.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Scoring pseudocode\n\n```pseudo\n# Setup (held fixed across criteria)\nmodel        \u2190 load(PRIMARY_BACKBONE)           # LLaMA-2-7B-Chat class\ntokenizer    \u2190 model.tokenizer\nseed         \u2190 SEED                              # single fixed int\nexemplars[t] \u2190 pick_3shot(BBH_DEV, task=t)       # deterministic per task\n\n# One pass over the eval split\nfor t in BBH_TASKS:                               # |T| = 27\n    for x in BBH_EVAL[t]:                         # <=250 per task\n        prompt \u2190 build_prompt(exemplars[t], x, cot=PROTOCOL)\n        if t in MCQ_23:\n            scores[c] \u2190 loglik_continuation(prompt + \" \" + c)  for c in OPTIONS[t]\n            pred_letter \u2190 argmax(scores)\n            raw_pred    \u2190 pred_letter\n            raw_gold    \u2190 gold_letter\n        else:                                      # Free-form 4\n            raw_pred \u2190 model.generate(prompt, greedy, seed, max_new, stop)\n            raw_gold \u2190 gold_text[x]\n\n        y_em    \u2190 score_em(raw_pred, raw_gold)\n        y_mined \u2190 score_mined(raw_pred, raw_gold)  # see below\n\n        # Both criteria run on the SAME (raw_pred, raw_gold) \u2192 paired\n        record[t][x] \u2190 (raw_pred, raw_gold, y_em, y_mined)\n\n# Criteria\nscore_em(p, g):\n    p \u2190 lowercase(strip(collapse_ws(p)))\n    g \u2190 lowercase(strip(collapse_ws(g)))\n    return int(p == g)\n\nscore_mined(p, g, theta=0.5):\n    p \u2190 lowercase(strip(collapse_ws(p)))\n    g \u2190 lowercase(strip(collapse_ws(g)))\n    if p == g or g == \"\":  return 1                  # identical or vacuous gold\n    D \u2190 levenshtein(p, g)                            # char-level\n    s \u2190 1 - D / max(len(p), len(g))\n    return int(s >= theta)\n```\n\n**Parser** (identical inputs to both criteria):\n\n```pseudo\nparse_freeform_pred(text):\n    m \u2190 regex.search(r\"[Tt]he answer is (?:is\\s+)?([^\\n\\.]+)\", text)\n    if m: return m.group(1)\n    nums \u2190 regex.findall(r\"-?\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?\", text)\n    if nums: return nums[-1]\n    return last_nonempty_line(text)\n```\n\nPairing guarantee: both `score_em` and `score_mined` receive the **same** `raw_pred` and `raw_gold` for each `(t, x)`. Decoding never re-runs.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Bootstrap / inference procedure\n\n- **Unit of resampling:** the 27 tasks (cluster bootstrap). Example-level bootstrap would understate uncertainty because prompts within a task are correlated.\n- **B = 10 000** resamples, seeded for reproducibility.\n- For resample `b`, draw tasks with replacement of size 27; recompute macro-accuracy under EM, under MinED, and the per-task \u0394.\n- Report: `acc_EM` point + 95 % CI (cluster-bootstrap percentile method); `acc_MinED` point + 95 % CI; **`\u0394 = acc_MinED \u2212 acc_EM` point + 95 % CI** (paired by construction \u2014 same resample indices).\n- **Non-parametric check:** Wilcoxon signed-rank over the 27 task-level \u0394s.\n- **Effect sizes:** median \u0394 across 27 task-\u0394s; **share of tasks where MinED > EM** (ties count as not-favoring per task).\n- **CoT vs no-CoT:** the no-CoT arm produces its own 3-tuple `(acc_EM, acc_MinED, \u0394)`; reported in a short paragraph rather than a parallel result table.\n\n---\n\n### 5. MCQ / Free-form decomposition tables (schema; no numbers invented)\n\n**Table 1 \u2014 Per-task layout (one row per task; 27 rows total).**\n\n| Task | Family | MCQ/FF | n_eval | acc_EM | acc_MinED | \u0394 = MinED \u2212 EM | disagreement count |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 27 names incl. `boolean_expressions`, `causal_judgement`, \u2026, `dyck_languages`, `multistep_arithmetic_two`, `object_counting`, `word_sorting` | logical / temporal / semantic / numeric / linguistic | MCQ-23 / FF-4 | exact | exact | exact | exact | exact |\n\nFree-form 4 per official BBH taxonomy: `dyck_languages`, `multistep_arithmetic_two`, `object_counting`, `word_sorting`.\n\n**Table 2 \u2014 Aggregations (primary deliverable).**\n\n| Aggregate | acc_EM [95 % CI] | acc_MinED [95 % CI] | \u0394 [95 % CI] | Median \u0394 | Tasks favoring MinED |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| All 27 (equal-weighted) | \u2026 | \u2026 | \u2026 | \u2026 | \u2026 |\n| All 27 (accuracy-then-macro, sensitivity) | \u2026 | \u2026 | \u2026 | \u2026 | \u2026 |\n| MCQ-23 (sub-aggregate) | \u2026 | \u2026 | \u2026 | \u2026 | \u2026 |\n| **Free-form-4 (sub-aggregate, decisive)** | \u2026 | \u2026 | \u2026 | \u2026 | \u2026 |\n\n**Table 3 \u2014 No-CoT sensitivity (paragraph form, not a parallel table).** One row of macro numbers for the 4 free-form tasks under no-CoT, paired \u0394 with CI.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Disagreement taxonomy\n\nFor every `(t, x)` where `y_em \u2260 y_mined`, classify the raw `pred` vs `gold` into exactly one bucket:\n\n1. **Punctuation / case** \u2014 `'42.'` vs `'42'`, `'Yes,'` vs `'yes'`. MinED rescues via similarity; EM fails.\n2. **Trailing units / qualifiers** \u2014 `'5 meters'` vs `'5'`, `'positive'` vs `'positive,'`. MinED rescues; EM fails.\n3. **Numeric rounding / formatting** \u2014 `'3.14'` vs `'3.140'`, `'1e2'` vs `'100'`. Often dataset-side inconsistency; reports per-task prevalence.\n4. **Paraphrase / near-miss** \u2014 `'cannot be determined'` vs `'indeterminate'`. Genuine semantic gap that MinED credits but humans may not.\n5. **Answer-extraction artifact** \u2014 parser chose trailing junk (e.g. `'7 because\u2026'`); category held identifiable by `(t, x)` so a manual spot-check can override.\n\nReport counts per bucket overall and per task. Surface categories (4) and (5) as **reviewer flags**, not silent winners \u2014 they are where MinED's relative gain may overstate semantic correctness.\n\n---\n\n### 7. Pre-registered decision rule (locked from item m)\n\n> **Question:** \"For Alignment Criteria, does the proposed MinED method outperform EM on BBH?\"\n>\n> **Decision rule.** Let `\u0394_macro` be the macro-averaged MinED \u2212 EM across the 27 tasks with cluster-bootstrap 95 % CI `CI_\u0394`. Let `\u0394_ff4` be the corresponding paired \u0394 on the **Free-form-4** sub-aggregate.\n>\n> - **Conclude `yes`** iff `0 \u2209 CI_\u0394` (any direction) **and** `\u0394_ff4 > 0` (MinED strictly higher on free-form). The first condition establishes *statistical* separation; the second enforces *where the criterion was motivated*.\n> - **Conclude `inconclusive`** iff `0 \u2208 CI_\u0394` **or** `\u0394_ff4 == 0` within resolution, even at strong MCQ deltas \u2014 **MCQ deltas alone cannot support `yes`**.\n> - **Conclude `no`** iff `\u0394_macro \u2264 0` with `CI_\u0394` excluding positive values **or** `\u0394_ff4 \u2264 0` decisively.\n>\n> All three branches are reported with: point estimates, CIs, Wilcoxon p, median \u0394, share-of-tasks-favoring-MinED, and the disagreement-bucket counts from \u00a76.\n\nThis rule embeds the (f)-induced asymmetry: a \"yes\" cannot ride on MCQ noise.\n\n---\n\n### 8. Feasibility statement\n\n- **Compute budget class:** one A-class GPU (~40 GB), bf16 / fp16 weights, \u226424 CPU workers; within the \"no budget specified \u2192 one-GPU-day class\" envelope.\n- **Cost estimate:** 27 tasks \u00d7 \u2264250 examples \u2248 6,750 generations \u00d7 1 primary model (\u2248600 tokens out average) \u2248 4 M generated tokens for the headline CoT arm; plus \u22642 secondary arms at the same footprint \u2192 roughly 1 GPU-day total per model. No-CoT is shorter and folds into the same day.\n- **Runtime checks at runner time** (not part of design itself): model fits in bf16; KV-cache supports max sequence length of the CoT prompt + 600 tokens; stop tokens include the BBH canonical set per task.\n- **Out of scope (explicit non-goals):** hyperparameter sweeps; MinED threshold sweep (\u03b8 fixed at 0.5 per h); character-vs-word Levenshtein sensitivity; tuning few-shot exemplars on the eval split; sampling-based decoding variance.\n- **What this document does NOT claim:** that any experiment was executed; that any number in \u00a75 was produced; that the chosen model's weights, the BBH eval split, or any paper-specific convention in the sandbox has been independently verified.\n\n---\n\n### 9. Repository / environment observations used\n\n- `inspect_repository /workspace` returned exactly one file, `/workspace/task.json`, with `question`, `context`, `documents.track.md = \"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\"`\n- No source paper PDF, no model checkpoint, no BBH data, no code were present. Every paper-specific convention (MinED formula, \u03b8, EM variant, MCQ scoring route, model identity) is therefore locked from the researcher's choices in this turn rather than recovered from local artifacts.\n- Sandbox constraints (bubblewrap, network off, no GPU, system Python, no preinstalled deps) preclude executing the design even if desired \u2014 consistent with the brief.\n\n---\n\n### 10. Final handoff statement\n\nThis is a **design document only**. The plan in the previous turn is **approved**; this document **locks** items (a)\u2013(m) into a single reproducible recipe, registers a decision rule with explicit handling of the (f)-induced MCQ-triviality, and is ready for a runner to execute against the researcher's preferred backbone and paper conventions. No execution is claimed here; no numbers are invented. The decision in \u00a77 will be populated only after the runner executes steps \u00a73\u2013\u00a76 on the eval split.", "evidence": "Workspace inspection confirmed only /workspace/task.json plus the track.md note \"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\" No paper PDF, no model weights, no BBH data, no code were shipped in /workspace. Researcher's locked choices (a)\u2013(m) cover every degree of freedom that would otherwise have required source-paper text: MinED formula and \u03b8=0.5 (h), EM variant (g), MCQ scoring route (f), model class (b), prompting regime (d), split (e), parser (i), aggregation (j), inference (k), disagreement taxonomy (l), and decision rule (m). This is a design-only task in a sandbox without compute or shipped artifacts, so no experiment can be or is claimed to have been executed; every figure in Tables 1\u20133 is left as a schema row to be populated by a runner.", "assumptions": ["Budget is unenforced by the brief; the design assumes a one-GPU-day envelope with at most 1 primary + 2 secondary arms and no hyperparameter sweeps.</item>\n<item>Cluster bootstrap resamples tasks with replacement at B=10000 and is seeded; the unit of independence is tasks, not examples.</item>\n<item>The free-form parser is held identical across both criteria so any criterion-level difference is attributable to the scoring rule and not the parser (locked choice i).</item>\n<item>The 3 few-shot exemplars are drawn from BBH dev exclusively; dev never overlaps with eval.</item>\n<item>Ties at \u03b8=0.5 count as correct for MinED (locked choice h, item A7 of the prior plan).</item>\n<item>MinED applies at the character level (locked convention); a word-level Levenshtein is noted as out-of-scope sensitivity, not part of the headline.</item>\n<item>Greedy decoding with a fixed seed is treated as deterministic; any backend non-determinism is a runtime flag for the runner, not a design re-run.</item>\n<item>BBH eval split is publicly distributable with at most 250 examples per task (headline figure about 6750); the design reports actual n_eval per task in Table 1 rather than asserting 250 universally.</item>\n<item>Primary backbone is approximately 7B-class instruction-tuned chat (LLaMA-2-7B-Chat class); selected so that bf16 weights plus KV-cache for prompt plus at most 600 generated tokens fit on a single ~40 GB GPU within the one-GPU-day envelope.</item>\n<item>All items (a)\u2013(m) from the researcher are locked and treated as fixed for the design; every paper-specific convention (MinED formula, threshold 0.5, EM normalization, MCQ likelihood-based scoring, free-form parser) is taken from the locked choice rather than re-derived from a source paper that is not present in this sandbox.</item>"], "uncertainties": ["Determinism guarantees of greedy decoding can vary by serving backend; the greedy+seed lock is necessary but its realization is left as a runtime check.</item>\n<item>Whether the chosen 7B backbone is exactly the one used in the paper is unknown; the design documents per-model \u0394 if multiple arms are run, so backbone-induced variation is at least visible.</item>\n<item>Item (f) implies MCQ delta is structurally near-zero because both criteria receive canonical option letters; the design accounts for this by requiring Free-form-4 to also favor MinED before concluding yes, but the magnitude of the MCQ residual gap (whitespace, casing of the option token) remains an empirical question.</item>\n<item>Whether the BBH eval split per-task count is exactly 250 for all 27 tasks in the public release is not verifiable locally; Table 1 reports the per-task n_eval the runner observes rather than asserting 250 universally.</item>\n<item>The exact paper definition of MinED (normalization unit, \u03b8) is not recoverable from this sandbox; the design uses the locked convention (char-level Levenshtein, \u03b8=0.5, ties count as correct) regardless, and any post-hoc paper-matching is the runner's responsibility.</item>"]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-b34acc41-f5e5-4b7a-b35f-b244c1090392", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 15}
